The policy uses a simple linear rule based on velocity: when the car’s velocity is negative the left‑push (action 0) gets the highest score, and when velocity is positive the right‑push (action 2) dominates. This mimics the classic bang‑bang strategy for MountainCar, alternating thrust to build momentum without relying on the idle action. By setting only the velocity weights (−1.0 for left, +1.0 for right) and zeroing other weights and biases, the controller reacts directly to the sign of the velocity, encouraging the necessary back‑and‑forth swings to reach the goal and should improve the return toward the target –120.
