The chosen weights implement a simple velocity‑sign controller: when the car’s velocity is negative the left‐action score (‑vel) exceeds the idle bias, producing a left push; when the velocity is positive the right‑action score ( +vel) dominates, yielding a right push. A small positive bias for the idle action ensures the car remains idle at zero velocity, preventing indecisive ties. This linear rule encourages the classic alternating left/right thrust needed to build momentum and escape the valley, increasing the chance of reaching the goal in fewer than 200 steps.
